# Clp at tier P0 — the recalibrated bottom rung, presolve on both sides.
#
# T0 with `-presolve off` removed and nothing else; the crash basis stays off
# and the dual stays forced, because JAOS still has neither a crash basis nor
# a primal. See highs-P0.opt for why T0 keeps its old definition.
#
# -dualsimplex is the verb rather than an option, so it comes last: Clp reads
# its arguments in order and the solve happens where the verb is. One token
# per line, because the harness passes these unquoted and Clp takes its
# options as separate -name value pairs.

-primalTolerance
1e-7
-dualTolerance
1e-7
-crash
off
-dualsimplex
